id: pm-55yf1t
title: "MCP 2026-07-28 conformance and release gate: official schema matrix, protocol-era adapters, real transports, adversarial cases, and published consumers"
description: "Build a requirement-complete test and release gate that proves the SDK, stdio server, Streamable HTTP server, packages, docs, and published artifacts implement the declared 2026-07-28 surface."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:mcp",ci,conformance,negative-control,published-artifact,real-process,release-gate
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:12:34.029Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T05:50:34.380Z"
deadline: "2026-12-15T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 1200
acceptance_criteria: "A generated matrix maps every official 2026-07-28 normative requirement and supported extension to owners and executable evidence with no unclassified row; Official schema fixtures and protocol-era tests run through the public SDK and real stdio and Streamable HTTP processes; Each major behavior has a negative control that demonstrates the gate fails when the behavior is removed or malformed; Concurrency, cancellation, disconnect, retry, replay, authorization, caching, resource bounds, and token ceilings have adversarial coverage; Packed, npm, npx, and bunx consumers execute the full canonical agent journey and verify the advertised protocol version; Release is refused if source, generated schemas, docs, contracts, server discovery, package metadata, or published behavior disagree"
goal: Evidence-backed MCP conformance
objective: "Turn every normative requirement and supported extension into executable local, hosted, packed, and published proof"
value: "Protocol drift, false-green tests, legacy regressions, security mistakes, and broken package bins fail before release"
why_now: The existing handshake test proves an obsolete revision and the release probe validates only initialize rather than the latest protocol and extensions
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: critical
confidence: high
